We've all felt shy, right? One time or another, most of us have felt awkward or worried in unfamiliar social situations. You might have children who hide behind your legs during an entire birthday party rather than play with the other kids. A 2011 report in the journal Pediatrics found that approximately half of all teenagers consider themselves shy. Shyness isn't a disorder, but it can make life difficult for children and adults. In this episode, we talk with a psychologist who has been helping shy people for more than 35 years. and tells us you can't really take the shyness out of people, but you can manage it, and it might not be as hard as you think.
我们都曾感到害羞，对吧？在某个时候，我们大多数人在陌生的人际交往中都曾感到尴尬或担忧。你可能见过这样的孩子：在整个生日派对期间，他们一直躲在你的腿后面，而不是和其它孩子一起玩。2011年《儿科学》杂志上的一份报告发现，大约有一半的青少年认为自己很害羞。害羞并不是一种失调症，但它确实会给儿童和成人的生活带来困难。在本期节目中，我们采访了一位帮助害羞人群超过35年的心理学家，他告诉我们，你无法真正消除人们的害羞，但你可以掌控它，而且这或许并没有你想象的那么难。

2
