The first thing they do when they look into a mirror is they primp. They focus on their hair. They adjust their tie, their color. They focus on their faults because a mirror makes you self-conscious. And when you're self-conscious, you focus on your negative characteristics. So we say, think about shy people as having a mirror held in front of them all day long, particularly in social situations. So that's what shyness, that's what shyness is.
