that, a big mistake that shy people make. A huge mistake is that if they're going to go to a social function, they think, okay, I'll show up late, party starts at nine, I'll get there at 1030, because there'll be lots of people there. I'll be able to mingle. Nobody will notice me because I can just kind of blend in. That's the worst thing that you can do. You do that because you don't understand the real dynamic. Rather than showing up late, what you should do is you show up early.
害羞的人常犯的一个巨大错误。一个极其严重的错误是，如果他们要去参加一个社交活动，他们会想：“好吧，我晚点去，派对九点开始，我十点半再去，因为那时候人会很多。我能够四处交际。没有人会注意到我，因为我可以融入其中。”这是你能做的最糟糕的事情。你之所以这么做，是因为你不理解真正的动态机制。你应该做的不是迟到，而是早到。

13
00:06:07.000 --> 00:06:29.000
When you show up late, the noise level is already high. So if you're anxious, that's going to make you even more anxious. Plus, if you have difficulty talking to people, if you show up late, people are already mingling together. groups have already started to form, so it's much harder to break into that group. So we say, don't show up late. You show up on time. Show up early.
当你迟到时，噪音水平已经很高了。所以如果你本来就很焦虑，这会让你更加焦虑。另外，如果你本来就不擅长与人交谈，当你迟到时，大家已经都在互相交际了，群体也已经开始形成，所以想要融入那个群体就困难得多了。因此我们说，不要迟到。你应该按时到场，甚至早到。

14
00:06:29.000 --> 00:07:04.000
So when you show up early, the noise level is low, so you can adapt to that noise level as it gets louder. You can meet people one-on-one when they come in. So you introduce yourself, and as other people come in, you introduce these people to others as well. You become the social facility. That's much easier to do. Another tip that we recommend is engage in a quick talk. Talk to lots of different kinds of people for very brief periods of time. The big mistake that shy people make is that they think that when they get into a conversation,
所以当你早到时，噪音水平很低，你就可以随着声音变得嘈杂而逐渐适应这种环境。当人们陆续进来时，你可以和他们进行一对一的交流。你可以做自我介绍，当其他人进来时，你也可以把这些人介绍给其他人。你成了社交的促进者。这要容易得多。我们推荐的另一个小建议是进行快速交谈。与形形色色的人进行非常简短的交谈。害羞的人犯的一个大错误是，他们认为当自己进入一段对话时，

15
