So they feel comfortable with that. And then what you can do is you can introduce another child into the familiar situation. So don't push things too quickly, give them time to adjust and engage in this factorial approach. That's what we do as adults as well. But again, a problem is because things are easy for us. We expect them to be easy for the child as well. well. So we get impatient. We push. We fail to consider that warm-up effect. So there's many things that that parents can do to help their child be social, deal with frustration tolerance.
所以他们对此感到适应。然后你可以做的是，在一个熟悉的环境中引入另一个孩子。所以不要把事情推得太快，给他们时间去调整并采用这种因子分析法。这也是我们作为成年人通常会做的事情。然而问题在于，因为很多事情对我们来说很容易，我们也期望它们对孩子来说同样容易。所以我们会失去耐心，会去催促，却忽略了那个热络效应。因此，父母可以做很多事情来帮助他们的孩子进行社交，应对挫折耐受力。

28
00:13:04.000 --> 00:13:36.000
We now live in the age of Instagram, Facebook, Snapchat. You know, communication is moving at lightning speed. How do you're talking about warming up, going getting into situations where they feel comfortable, but how do shy people keep up in these situations? First and foremost, what we have to remember always, and it's been this way forever, okay? First and foremost, we have to remember that it takes all kinds of people to make this world work. It takes people who are going to move really, really fast.
我们现在生活在Instagram、Facebook、Snapchat的时代。你知道，信息传播的速度快如闪电。你刚才谈到了热络起来，进入让他们感到舒适的环境，但在这种情况下，害羞的人该如何跟上节奏呢？首先也是最重要的一点，我们必须永远记住——而且情况一直如此——首先也是最重要的一点，我们要记住，世界要运转需要形形色色的人。我们需要行动非常非常快的人，

29
00:13:36.000 --> 00:14:02.000
It's going to take people who are going to move really, really slow, and it's going to take a lot of people in between. So we say it's not necessary that everybody keep up with that same pace, so we tell shy people, find the pace that that's comfortable for you. Go to your strengths. And what's going to happen is as you begin to build on these kinds of things, as you begin to feel more comfortable, you'll pick up the pace that's comfortable for you. I mean, think about driving on the interstate.
我们需要行动非常非常慢的人，还需要介于两者之间的许多人。所以我们说，并非每个人都必须保持完全相同的节奏，我们告诉害羞的人：找到适合你自己的节奏。发挥你的优势。随着你开始在这些方面不断积累，随着你开始感到更加舒适，你会找到适合你自己的节奏。我的意思是，想想在州际公路上开车。

30
00:14:02.000 --> 00:14:27.000
If everybody drove really, really fast, it would be impossible. If everybody drove really slow, it would be impossible. You need all kinds of different drivers to make this work. Some fast, some slow, and a lot in between. and the same is in digital technology. So again, there's no need for everybody to do everything the same way. What we need is diversity. And shy people truly represent that.
如果所有人都开得非常非常快，那将是不可能的。如果所有人都开得很慢，那也将是不可能的。你需要各种不同类型的司机来让交通顺畅运转。有些快，有些慢，还有许多介于两者之间。在数字技术中也是如此。所以同样，没有必要让每个人都以相同的方式做所有事情。我们需要的是多样性。而害羞的人恰恰代表了这一点。

